==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
The term was coined in 1848 by [[w:Rudolf Virchow|Rudolf Virchow]] From {{bor|en|la|embolus|t=piston}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἔμβολος|t=peg, stopper}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɛmbələs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|emboli|+}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} An obstruction causing an [[embolism]]: a [[blood clot]], air bubble or other matter carried by the [[bloodstream]] and causing a blockage or [[occlusion]] of a [[blood vessel]].
# {{lb|en|zoology}} The structure on the end of the [[palp]] of male arachnids which contains the opening to the ejaculatory duct.
#* '''1996''', Michael J Roberts, ''Spiders of Britain and Northern Europe'', Collins 1996, p. 22:
#*: Those spiders with a simple bulb insert most of this; those with a complex palp insert only the '''embolus''', which in some species is very long {{...}}

